{
  "created": "2026-08-25",
  "target": "live theme — Impact, sections/footer-group.json, section 'brand_layout_css' (custom-html)",
  "decided_by": "Malcolm, 2026-08-25 — 'for all of the solution pages: remove the carousel function from the content blocks, so that the content blocks are all shown on the page'",
  "note": "The Skin Solutions pages were never given a carousel on purpose. They inherited one.\n\nThe homepage reviews slider is built in the footer-group custom-html block, because media-with-text is the only section in Impact that gives image-left / quote-right and it renders no carousel controls at all. That slider was scoped by BLOCK COUNT: the CSS turned any `.media-with-text` with six or more `__item` children into a 100%-wide scroll-snapping track, and the JS injected prev/next arrows on the same test. footer-group renders on every page of the store, so the rule is evaluated everywhere.\n\nSix sections on this store have six or more blocks. One is the reviews slider. The other five are the `content` sections of the five Skin Solutions pages, each of which carries exactly six editorial blocks — intro, causes, approach and three product blocks. All five were being collapsed to a single visible block with the remaining five behind a horizontal scroll.\n\n  templates/index.json                       reviews   6 blocks  <- the intended slider\n  templates/page.brightening-glow.json       content   6 blocks  <- collateral\n  templates/page.collagen-skin-plumping.json content   6 blocks  <- collateral\n  templates/page.fine-lines-wrinkles.json    content   6 blocks  <- collateral\n  templates/page.firming-skin-density.json   content   6 blocks  <- collateral\n  templates/page.skin-repair-renewal.json    content   6 blocks  <- collateral\n\nThis is the second bug from the same root cause in two days. fix-stray-slider-arrows.json (2026-08-25) made the JS threshold agree with the CSS at six; both were still counting blocks, which is a proxy for the reviews slider rather than a description of it, and the proxy was wrong for five pages.\n\nTHE FIX IS THE SELECTOR, NOT THE COUNT. Both the CSS and the JS now ask whether the section contains the 'See All Customer Reviews' link, a[href$=\"/pages/reviews\"], which is what is actually unique to the reviews slider. Checked against all 57 live templates: 22 media-with-text sections exist and that link appears in exactly one of them. `$=` rather than `=` so a Langify locale prefix (/de/pages/reviews) still matches and the slider keeps working on translated storefronts.\n\nWHY NOT SCOPE BY SECTION ID OR TEMPLATE. Section ids render as shopify-section-template--<theme id>__<key> and go stale on every theme copy; footer-group has no access to the current template, and custom-html rejects Liquid. Section content is the only stable discriminator available from a sitewide style block.\n\nNOTHING ELSE IN THE BLOCK CHANGES. The whole html value is carried here verbatim so the diff is auditable and the push is a straight replacement — same convention as fix-stray-slider-arrows.json.",
  "expected_result": {
    "solution_pages": "All six content blocks stack vertically, alternating image left / image right (alternate_media_position is true on all five). No arrows, no horizontal scroll.",
    "homepage": "Reviews slider unchanged — six slides, scroll-snap, always-visible prev/next arrows, outline button hover.",
    "research_and_philosophy_pages": "Unchanged — their 3-block Key Findings sections fell below the old threshold and fall outside the new selector too."
  },
